readme.text:
A live session cannot be pulled out from under its Agent, so the second option
queues it instead:

- the id is written to `~/.dsh/plugin-session-delete/pending.json`;
- the session is archived (best effort) so the row disappears from the default
  list;
- the next DeepSeek Harness start retries the removal, when the write handle is
  free;
- **unarchiving the session cancels its queued removal** — the archive is the
  visible "pending removal" state.

- **attachments** — content-addressed under `~/.dsh/attachments` and possibly
  shared with other sessions;
- **subagent child sessions** — separate ids, hidden from the sidebar by design;
  delete them individually;
- **the SQLite search index**, if your composition uses
  `dsh-session-query-sqlite` — it reconciles deleted sources on the next search;
- **derived rows in other domains** (telemetry, titles) — they are keyed by an
  id that no longer resolves and are ignored.
